      "right": 0.945,
      "bottom": 0.028333333333333332,
      "top": 0.045
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Necessary payload",
      "left": 0.083,
      "right": 0.266671875,
      "bottom": 0.6748888888888889,
      "top": 0.706
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Fields are needed for the\nresult or later computation.\nAn ordinary helper read\ncounts, even without Visit.",
      "left": 0.083,
      "right": 0.28628125,
      "bottom": 0.5256666666666667,
      "top": 0.645
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Filter-only payload",
      "left": 0.38299999999999995,
      "right": 0.567375,
      "bottom": 0.6748888888888889,
      "top": 0.706
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Full node fetched only to\nreject it using a predicate.\nSQL can evaluate the filter\nwithout returning the node.",
      "left": 0.38299999999999995,
      "right": 0.586515625,
      "bottom": 0.5256666666666667,
      "top": 0.645
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Unused prefetch",
      "left": 0.6830000000000002,
      "right": 0.8454218750000001,
      "bottom": 0.6748888888888889,
      "top": 0.706
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Payload returned by the\nprefetch worker, but never\nread by foreground code.\nThis is also avoidable.",
      "left": 0.6830000000000002,
      "right": 0.8808125000000001,
      "bottom": 0.5256666666666667,
      "top": 0.645
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "Confirmed unnecessary prefetch = unused + disjoint filter-only payloads",
      "left": 0.07,
      "right": 0.8921875,
      "bottom": 0.32555555555555554,
      "top": 0.36
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "The database still needs to evaluate predicates. We count complete node payloads transferred /\nmaterialized at the client, not PostgreSQL rows scanned or bytes read from disk.",
      "left": 0.06,
      "right": 0.814609375,
      "bottom": 0.19244444444444442,
      "top": 0.25
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "text": "A zero in the confirmed-count table means \u201cnone found in these two classes\u201d; it is not a proof\nthat all remaining full payloads or properties are semantically necessary.",
      "left": 0.06,
      "right": 0.715234375,
      "bottom": 0.102,
      "top": 0.15
    },
